, "No public general-election polling in the race"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point firmly to Bergman: an R+11 district, incumbency, and a near-unanimous Safe/Solid R expert consensus, with markets pricing the Democrat at only about 15%. Barr's solid fundraising and modest outside spending against Bergman justify only a small nudge toward the Democrat from the baseline.", "watch": "A late wave of Democratic outside spending or polling showing Barr within single digits would signal the race is more competitive than rated.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Jack Bergman (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Northern Michigan's 1st District is a solidly Republican seat that incumbent Jack Bergman, a retired Marine general, has held since 2017. Democrat Callie Barr, making her second attempt, has run a well-funded campaign and drawn local media attention, but the district's R+11 lean and Bergman's incumbency remain steep obstacles. Expert raters nearly unanimously call the race Safe or Solid Republican, with a couple of Likely Republican ratings, and prediction markets give the Democrat roughly a 15 percent chance.\n\nBarr's fundraising edge in cash on hand and some outside spending against Bergman suggest Democrats see a path, but no public polling has emerged to substantiate a real contest. The forecast expects Bergman to win by a double-digit margin, with modest uncertainty given the absence of polls.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0479, "margin": -11.4}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0291, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0616, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0563, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0486, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0433, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0528, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0342, "margin": -13.0